# Frontend implementation

App: `apps/hospital-portal-web` (Next.js App Router). Keep domain code in existing folders. Do not create new top-level architectural trees.

## Fast implementation boundary

For a FAST task, inspect only: the target route/component, its direct domain components, the relevant API/hook, applicable rules, and one representative implementation. Do not search the whole frontend unless a dependency is genuinely unresolved.

Prefer existing `src/components/ui`, `src/components/<domain>`, `src/app/<route>`, `src/lib`, hooks, stores, and API clients. Do not create a new abstraction merely to avoid reading an existing one.

## Data and state

TanStack Query is the server/cache layer. Reuse existing API modules and hooks. Auth/session uses `auth-store.ts` + permission cache. Clinical state uses existing clinical/domain providers. Do not create duplicate stores, raw fetch clients, or alternate auth/data libraries.

## Module homes

Counsellor → `components/counsellors-desk` and existing counselling routes. Patient/MPI → `components/patients`. Examination → `components/examination`. Imaging → `components/imaging` with Cornerstone lazy-loaded. Inventory → `/admin/inventory/*`. Notifications → existing SignalR notification hub + `react-hot-toast`.

## Performance

Preserve existing lazy/dynamic loading. Avoid duplicate SignalR subscriptions and refetch storms. Do not perform broad performance rewrites without measurement. Keep heavy widgets out of the global shell.

## Completion boundary

Implement only the requested scope. Do not refactor unrelated files, rename routes, migrate components, or perform opportunistic cleanup. Once acceptance criteria and targeted validation are satisfied, stop.
